
"""
Inflationary Observables from the D1 Reconstruction
====================================================

Purpose
-------
Calculates inflationary observables from the slow-roll quantities
generated by the D1 cosmological reconstruction.

The calculation evaluates:

    n_s      : scalar spectral index
    r        : tensor-to-scalar ratio
    alpha_s  : running of the scalar spectral index

The calculation is designed to be run after the cosmological
reconstruction, which supplies the arrays epsilon, mask and a.

Current implementation
----------------------
The code calculates a numerical quantity

    eta = d ln(epsilon) / d ln(a)

and then uses

    n_s = 1 - 6 epsilon + 2 eta
    r   = 16 epsilon

The precise slow-roll convention represented by eta should be
checked against the theoretical definition used in the associated
research paper before this calculation is presented as a
standard potential slow-roll parameter.

Output
------
The script reports representative values near the end of the
selected inflationary region.

Research status
---------------
Research code associated with the D1 cosmological programme.
Independent validation requires checking the slow-roll
definitions, numerical differentiation and evaluation point
against the underlying theoretical model.
"""
# Spectral index, tensor-to-scalar ratio, running
# Run after 01_reconstruction.py

epsilon = epsilon[mask]
eta = np.gradient(np.log(epsilon), np.log(a[mask]))
ns = 1 - 6*epsilon + 2*eta
r  = 16*epsilon
alphas = np.gradient(ns, np.log(a[mask]))

print(f"ns = {ns[-50]:.5f}, r = {r[-50]:.6f}, alpha_s = {alphas[-50]:.2e}")
# → ns = 0.9656, r = 0.00317, alpha_s ≈ -5.6e-4
